1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,440
A family in Karnataka asks a contractor one simple

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:07,302
question: how much will our house cost?

3
00:00:07,502 --> 00:00:09,755
He says ₹25 lakh.

4
00:00:09,955 --> 00:00:13,246
Eighteen months later, they've spent about ₹30 lakh.

5
00:00:13,446 --> 00:00:15,100
Here's the strange part.

6
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,493
Nobody lied to them.

7
00:00:16,493 --> 00:00:18,919
Nobody ran away with the money.

8
00:00:19,119 --> 00:00:21,427
So where did ₹5 lakh go?

9
00:00:21,627 --> 00:00:23,843
Today we're going to find every rupee.

10
00:00:23,843 --> 00:00:25,423
There are seven leaks.

11
00:00:25,623 --> 00:00:28,674
And leak number seven isn't made of cement or

12
00:00:28,674 --> 00:00:30,285
steel. It's made of paper,

13
00:00:30,285 --> 00:00:32,908
and it can stop your bank loan cold.

14
00:00:33,108 --> 00:00:34,128
Stay till the end,

15
00:00:34,128 --> 00:00:37,117
because we'll give you the six questions that plug

16
00:00:37,117 --> 00:00:38,387
every one of them.

17
00:00:39,837 --> 00:00:43,330
Every house quote in India starts with one formula.

18
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:46,362
Built-up area, times a rate per square foot.

19
00:00:46,562 --> 00:00:51,156
1,000 sq ft, at ₹2,500 a square foot.

20
00:00:51,156 --> 00:00:52,718
₹25 lakh.

21
00:00:52,918 --> 00:00:57,810
Basic homes are often quoted around ₹1,800 to ₹2,300

22
00:00:57,810 --> 00:00:58,901
a square foot.

23
00:00:59,101 --> 00:01:01,659
Standard, up to about ₹2,900.

24
00:01:01,659 --> 00:01:03,149
Premium, above that.

25
00:01:03,349 --> 00:01:06,192
That number feels like the price of your house.

26
00:01:06,392 --> 00:01:09,187
It isn't. It's the price of what's inside the

27
00:01:09,187 --> 00:01:12,406
contractor's rate. And a lot of your house lives

28
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:13,418
outside it.

29
00:01:14,868 --> 00:01:17,195
Leak one is hiding in the word area.

30
00:01:17,395 --> 00:01:20,314
Contractors usually quote on built-up area:

31
00:01:20,314 --> 00:01:22,503
every floor, including the walls,

32
00:01:22,503 --> 00:01:24,780
the balcony and the staircase.

33
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:26,761
But you live in carpet area,

34
00:01:26,761 --> 00:01:29,029
the floor you can actually walk on.

35
00:01:29,029 --> 00:01:30,817
And it's always smaller.

36
00:01:31,017 --> 00:01:33,463
So when two quotes say the same rate,

37
00:01:33,463 --> 00:01:34,981
ask: rate on which area?

38
00:01:34,981 --> 00:01:37,002
Get the answer in writing.

39
00:01:37,202 --> 00:01:39,419
It sounds small. On a full house,

40
00:01:39,419 --> 00:01:41,797
it changes the total by lakhs.

41
00:01:43,247 --> 00:01:44,737
Leak two is the biggest,

42
00:01:44,737 --> 00:01:45,850
and it's a list.

43
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:48,670
Plan approval fees. Before anyone digs,

44
00:01:48,670 --> 00:01:50,635
the plan has to be sanctioned,

45
00:01:50,635 --> 00:01:52,277
and that costs money.

46
00:01:52,477 --> 00:01:54,704
Soil test and structural design.

47
00:01:54,704 --> 00:01:56,850
Someone has to check the ground,

48
00:01:56,850 --> 00:01:58,997
and design what stands on it.

49
00:01:59,197 --> 00:02:00,848
Compound wall and gate.

50
00:02:00,848 --> 00:02:03,445
Borewell, sump and overhead tank.

51
00:02:03,645 --> 00:02:05,066
Every plot needs them.

52
00:02:05,066 --> 00:02:06,723
But none of them are rooms,

53
00:02:06,723 --> 00:02:08,697
so none of them fit in a rate per

54
00:02:08,697 --> 00:02:09,736
square foot.

55
00:02:09,936 --> 00:02:12,223
Electricity and water connections.

56
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:14,637
You can't live in a house without them.

57
00:02:14,637 --> 00:02:16,805
They still sit outside the rate.

58
00:02:17,005 --> 00:02:19,179
Interiors: the modular kitchen,

59
00:02:19,179 --> 00:02:22,440
the wardrobes. The things that make it feel like

60
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:23,024
home.

61
00:02:23,224 --> 00:02:26,243
And GST, if it wasn't already in the quote.

62
00:02:26,443 --> 00:02:27,864
None of these are tricks.

63
00:02:27,864 --> 00:02:30,885
They're just not inside the per-square-foot rate.

64
00:02:31,085 --> 00:02:33,635
And most quotes simply don't mention them,

65
00:02:33,635 --> 00:02:36,661
so nobody counts them until the bills arrive.

66
00:02:36,861 --> 00:02:39,618
In our example, they add up to about ₹3

67
00:02:39,618 --> 00:02:40,183
lakh.

68
00:02:40,383 --> 00:02:42,575
Three lakh that was never in the quote.

69
00:02:42,775 --> 00:02:45,995
And then there's the money every builder needs and

70
00:02:45,995 --> 00:02:48,680
almost nobody budgets: a contingency.

71
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,366
Usually 5 to 10 percent,

72
00:02:51,366 --> 00:02:54,379
for price rises and the changes you'll make along

73
00:02:54,379 --> 00:02:55,081
the way.

74
00:02:55,281 --> 00:02:57,139
Because you will make changes.

75
00:02:57,139 --> 00:02:58,402
A bigger window here.

76
00:02:58,402 --> 00:02:59,841
Better tiles there.

77
00:03:00,041 --> 00:03:04,011
At 8 percent, that's another ₹2,24,000.

78
00:03:04,211 --> 00:03:06,637
₹25 lakh just became ₹30 lakh.

79
00:03:08,087 --> 00:03:10,592
Now the leaks that can push you past thirty.

80
00:03:10,792 --> 00:03:12,429
Leak three is the soil.

81
00:03:12,629 --> 00:03:15,704
Across north Karnataka, a lot of land sits on

82
00:03:15,704 --> 00:03:18,778
black cotton soil. It swells when it's wet and

83
00:03:18,778 --> 00:03:20,480
shrinks when it's dry.

84
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,737
Build on it like normal ground,

85
00:03:22,737 --> 00:03:23,971
and you get cracks.

86
00:03:23,971 --> 00:03:25,369
Build on it properly,

87
00:03:25,369 --> 00:03:27,676
and the foundation costs more.

88
00:03:27,876 --> 00:03:30,343
That's why a soil test isn't paperwork.

89
00:03:30,343 --> 00:03:33,883
It's the cheapest insurance in the whole project.

90
00:03:35,333 --> 00:03:37,117
Leak four happens quietly,

91
00:03:37,117 --> 00:03:38,746
at the material yard.

92
00:03:38,946 --> 00:03:42,416
Nobody hides anything. The quote is just vague.

93
00:03:42,616 --> 00:03:44,943
Your quote says cement.

94
00:03:44,943 --> 00:03:47,882
But which cement? 33,

95
00:03:47,882 --> 00:03:51,189
43 or 53 grade?

96
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:52,419
OPC or PPC?

97
00:03:52,619 --> 00:03:55,010
PPC is usually a little cheaper per bag,

98
00:03:55,010 --> 00:03:57,277
and both are fine when used right.

99
00:03:57,477 --> 00:03:59,233
Your quote says steel.

100
00:03:59,233 --> 00:04:03,234
But which TMT? Fe 500 or 500D?

101
00:04:03,234 --> 00:04:04,460
Which brand?

102
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:06,486
Each choice changes the price.

103
00:04:06,486 --> 00:04:09,043
And a quote that just says cement and steel

104
00:04:09,043 --> 00:04:11,704
doesn't tell you which one you're getting.

105
00:04:11,904 --> 00:04:14,735
And it doesn't stop at cement and steel.

106
00:04:14,735 --> 00:04:18,114
Tiles, paint, wires and pipes all come in cheap

107
00:04:18,114 --> 00:04:19,916
and costly versions.

108
00:04:20,116 --> 00:04:22,928
Once they're inside a wall or under a floor,

109
00:04:22,928 --> 00:04:24,168
they look the same.

110
00:04:24,168 --> 00:04:25,989
Until one of them fails.

111
00:04:26,189 --> 00:04:28,990
If the quote doesn't name the brand and grade,

112
00:04:28,990 --> 00:04:32,102
two contractors can quote the same price for two

113
00:04:32,102 --> 00:04:33,830
very different houses.

114
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:35,361
Same rate on paper.

115
00:04:35,361 --> 00:04:36,942
Not the same house.

116
00:04:37,142 --> 00:04:39,341
So ask for an itemised quote:

117
00:04:39,341 --> 00:04:41,349
brand and grade of cement,

118
00:04:41,349 --> 00:04:44,658
steel, tiles, paint, wiring and plumbing.

119
00:04:44,858 --> 00:04:47,580
Line by line, so every number has a name

120
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:48,532
next to it.

121
00:04:48,732 --> 00:04:50,904
Now you're comparing the same house.

122
00:04:52,354 --> 00:04:54,210
Leak five is the most painful,

123
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:56,239
because you pay for it twice.

124
00:04:56,439 --> 00:04:59,101
When concrete isn't vibrated properly,

125
00:04:59,101 --> 00:05:00,930
it leaves gaps and pockets.

126
00:05:00,930 --> 00:05:03,426
Engineers call it honeycombing.

127
00:05:03,626 --> 00:05:06,708
And concrete that dries too fast never reaches its

128
00:05:06,708 --> 00:05:07,838
full strength.

129
00:05:08,038 --> 00:05:09,877
That's why it has to be cured,

130
00:05:09,877 --> 00:05:11,297
kept wet, for days.

131
00:05:11,497 --> 00:05:15,182
India's concrete code asks for at least 7 days

132
00:05:15,182 --> 00:05:19,724
with ordinary cement, and 10 with blended cements like

133
00:05:19,724 --> 00:05:20,231
PPC.

134
00:05:20,431 --> 00:05:22,925
Skip it, and the repair bill arrives later.

135
00:05:22,925 --> 00:05:24,055
With interest.

136
00:05:25,505 --> 00:05:27,852
Leak six shows up a year after you move

137
00:05:27,852 --> 00:05:28,253
in.

138
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:30,797
White, powdery patches on the walls.

139
00:05:30,797 --> 00:05:34,765
It's called efflorescence: salts carried up by moisture.

140
00:05:34,965 --> 00:05:37,899
A thin damp-proof course at plinth level helps stop

141
00:05:37,899 --> 00:05:38,987
that moisture.

142
00:05:39,187 --> 00:05:41,834
Leave it out, and you'll be repainting the same

143
00:05:41,834 --> 00:05:43,300
wall again and again.

144
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:46,014
And now, leak seven.

145
00:05:46,014 --> 00:05:47,697
The one made of paper.

146
00:05:47,897 --> 00:05:50,861
In Karnataka, the khata says your property is on

147
00:05:50,861 --> 00:05:51,719
the books.

148
00:05:51,919 --> 00:05:55,399
An A-khata is what banks are most comfortable lending

149
00:05:55,399 --> 00:05:59,275
against. B-khata properties can run into trouble with loans

150
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:00,474
and approvals.

151
00:06:00,674 --> 00:06:04,261
In Bengaluru, an e-khata is now needed to register

152
00:06:04,261 --> 00:06:05,318
a property.

153
00:06:05,518 --> 00:06:07,486
Then comes the sanctioned plan.

154
00:06:07,486 --> 00:06:08,319
And at the end,

155
00:06:08,319 --> 00:06:10,310
the occupancy certificate.

156
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:13,073
Many cities ask for it before they give you

157
00:06:13,073 --> 00:06:14,787
permanent connections.

158
00:06:14,987 --> 00:06:16,194
Get the paper wrong,

159
00:06:16,194 --> 00:06:19,060
and the cheapest house in the world can become

160
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:20,818
the one you can't finance.

161
00:06:21,018 --> 00:06:22,910
Can't sell. And can't finish.

162
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:27,196
So here are the six questions that plug every

163
00:06:27,196 --> 00:06:27,753
leak.

164
00:06:27,953 --> 00:06:30,597
One: rate on built-up or carpet area?

165
00:06:30,797 --> 00:06:33,039
Two: what's not included in this rate?

166
00:06:33,239 --> 00:06:35,273
Three: has the soil been tested?

167
00:06:35,473 --> 00:06:38,582
Four: which brand and grade of every material?

168
00:06:38,782 --> 00:06:41,463
Five: who checks the concrete and the curing?

169
00:06:41,663 --> 00:06:44,619
Six: are the khata and the plan sanction clear?

170
00:06:44,819 --> 00:06:46,465
Ask these before you sign,

171
00:06:46,465 --> 00:06:50,163
and ₹25 lakh stays closer to ₹25 lakh.

172
00:06:50,363 --> 00:06:54,868
Prices, calculators and checklists for your district are on

173
00:06:54,868 --> 00:06:56,289
buynbuild.blog.
